1
00:00:03,849 --> 00:00:06,294
The Lives of the Prophets Part 1;

2
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:10,428
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:11,071 --> 00:00:18,804
And then after this introduction of Da'wah(دعوة); after he has fulfilled his part in conveying to them the message,

4
00:00:18,971 --> 00:00:20,876
now he gets to the answer of the question.

5
00:00:21,852 --> 00:00:27,414
But he held them back until they finished delivering the message of truth to them.

6
00:00:27,827 --> 00:00:29,424
And now he's going to tell them the answer.

7
00:00:29,454 --> 00:00:29,866
Why?

8
00:00:29,896 --> 00:00:30,856
Because they need him.

9
00:00:31,303 --> 00:00:33,930
And because they need him, they're willing to, to listen.

10
00:00:34,303 --> 00:00:37,883
So he took advantage of that and he started giving them these important concepts,

11
00:00:38,065 --> 00:00:40,322
and now he's gonna give them the interpretation of the dream.

12
00:00:40,695 --> 00:00:41,290
He said;

13
00:00:41,750 --> 00:01:10,595
يا صاحِبَيِ السِّجنِ أَمّا أَحَدُكُما فَيَسقي رَبَّهُ خَمرًا ۖ وَأَمَّا الآخَرُ فَيُصلَبُ فَتَأكُلُ الطَّيرُ مِن رَأسِهِ ۚ

14
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,047
Oh two companions of the prison;

15
00:01:13,357 --> 00:01:21,269
As for one of you, he will pour out wine for his Lord, to drink,

16
00:01:21,714 --> 00:01:26,230
and as for the other; he will be crucified and birds will eat from his head.

17
00:01:26,519 --> 00:01:31,011
Thus is the case judged concerning what you both did inquire.

18
00:01:32,082 --> 00:01:35,885
One of you will be very close to the king.

19
00:01:36,266 --> 00:01:41,748
One of you is going to leave from this prison and jail and he is going to be one of the close associates of the king

20
00:01:41,835 --> 00:01:44,224
and he will be pouring wine for the king.

21
00:01:44,914 --> 00:01:46,796
This is the one who saw that he's pressing wine.

22
00:01:48,105 --> 00:01:52,907
And the other one of you will be taken out of jail and will be crucified

23
00:01:53,161 --> 00:01:56,913
and he will be left on the cross until birds will come and eat from his head.

24
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:02,484
And that is the one who saw that he has bread and birds are eating from it.

25
00:02:02,643 --> 00:02:03,253
And then he said;

26
00:02:03,413 --> 00:02:14,158
قُضِيَ الأَمرُ الَّذي فيهِ تَستَفتِيانِ۝

27
00:02:14,741 --> 00:02:17,095
The issue which you're asking about is judged; that's it.

28
00:02:17,206 --> 00:02:19,039
That's the judgment of Allah; it's done.

29
00:02:19,484 --> 00:02:26,350
And then SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) went to the one who he thought would be saved, and will be close to the king

30
00:02:26,627 --> 00:02:28,082
and SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) told him;

31
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:32,744
Please remember my name in front of the king.

32
00:02:34,315 --> 00:02:38,506
Yusuf(يوسُف) was thrown in jail, they oppressed him,

33
00:02:40,434 --> 00:02:44,042
so he appeal because the one who put him in jail was Al-Aziz(ألعزيز),

34
00:02:44,399 --> 00:02:46,764
and that was the second highest authority after the king.

35
00:02:47,336 --> 00:02:52,536
So there is no one; whom Yusuf(يوسُف) could appeal to; except the king, he is the next higher authority.

36
00:02:53,210 --> 00:02:56,345
So Yusuf(يوسُف) wanted his case to be presented in front of the king,

37
00:02:56,607 --> 00:03:00,974
so that the king would look into that case, and maybe, he would free him.

38
00:03:02,443 --> 00:03:03,369
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

39
00:03:03,399 --> 00:03:35,469
وَقالَ لِلَّذي ظَنَّ أَنَّهُ ناجٍ مِنهُمَا اذكُرني عِندَ رَبِّكَ فَأَنساهُ الشَّيطانُ ذِكرَ رَبِّهِ فَلَبِثَ فِي السِّجنِ بِضعَ سِنينَ۝

40
00:03:35,818 --> 00:03:39,725
And he said to the one whom he knew to be saved, mentioned me to your Lord

41
00:03:39,755 --> 00:03:41,022
Your Lord means your king.

42
00:03:42,548 --> 00:03:46,547
There are two interpretations given to the next part.

43
00:03:46,888 --> 00:03:49,721
فَأَنساهُ الشَّيطانُ ذِكرَ رَبِّهِ

44
00:03:50,332 --> 00:03:53,759
Satan made him forget to mention it to His Lord.

45
00:03:54,069 --> 00:03:55,473
There are two interpretations given;

46
00:03:55,838 --> 00:03:57,271
One interpretation is that

47
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:01,683
this man he left jail and he went to work with the king;

48
00:04:02,008 --> 00:04:08,993
but when he got in the palace and he gotten close to the king and all of the luxury of life, he forgot about Yusuf عليه السّلام.

49
00:04:09,771 --> 00:04:13,462
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) made him forget, that's one meaning.

50
00:04:14,502 --> 00:04:16,762
The other meaning is that;

51
00:04:17,182 --> 00:04:26,294
Sayidina Yusuf عليه السلام, forgot to ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and he asked this man to ask the king.

52
00:04:27,874 --> 00:04:30,921
Instead of asking Allah, he asked the king to help him.

53
00:04:32,159 --> 00:04:33,469
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) made him forget.

54
00:04:34,715 --> 00:04:37,654
And they say in the books of Tafseer(تفسير), some Mufasireen(مفسرين) say;

55
00:04:38,384 --> 00:04:42,809
that Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) came to see the Sadyina Yusuf عليه السّلام and told him;

56
00:04:42,839 --> 00:04:45,008
Who is the one, who freed you from the well.?

57
00:04:45,436 --> 00:04:46,486
He said: Allah;

58
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,401
Who is the one, who delivered you to safety in Egypt.?

59
00:04:49,648 --> 00:04:50,545
He said: Allah;

60
00:04:50,926 --> 00:04:54,870
Who is the one, who put you in the right place to be raised up and honored you?

61
00:04:55,068 --> 00:04:55,941
He said: Allah;

62
00:04:56,101 --> 00:04:59,365
Who is the one who saved you from the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of the wife of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز)?

63
00:04:59,453 --> 00:05:00,262
He said: Allah;

64
00:05:00,429 --> 00:05:03,397
He said: If Allah is the One, Who saved you throughout all of this.

65
00:05:03,603 --> 00:05:08,044
How come instead of asking Allah; you're asking the king to save you out of jail.

66
00:05:10,377 --> 00:05:14,780
And because of that mistake, he paid a price.

67
00:05:15,447 --> 00:05:16,471
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

68
00:05:16,501 --> 00:05:18,534
فَلَبِثَ فِي السِّجنِ بِضعَ سِنينَ۝

69
00:05:18,989 --> 00:05:21,597
He spent a few more years in jail.

70
00:05:22,853 --> 00:05:29,710
This mistake that seems to be small, he paid the price for it and he spent a few more years in jail.

71
00:05:30,878 --> 00:05:33,883
Ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى directly; He's the one who saved you throughout this.

72
00:05:34,232 --> 00:05:36,668
Now definitely SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) was asking Allah for Dua(دُعَا)

73
00:05:36,772 --> 00:05:40,215
but because he went through this human being and thought that he could do something;

74
00:05:40,437 --> 00:05:43,802
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants to teach him the lesson

75
00:05:44,318 --> 00:05:46,848
and the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى whenever they commit a mistake;

76
00:05:46,908 --> 00:05:52,260
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى teaches them, so that they would leave us a message that is clean,

77
00:05:52,768 --> 00:05:55,011
the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah when they commit mistakes;

78
00:05:55,185 --> 00:05:58,153
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى would correct their mistakes for them.

79
00:05:59,177 --> 00:06:03,964
So that when they Die all of the message that they leave behind is pure without any mistakes.

80
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:06,203
If there was anything in it; it would have been corrected.

81
00:06:08,671 --> 00:06:10,521
فَلَبِثَ فِي السِّجنِ بِضعَ سِنينَ۝

82
00:06:10,551 --> 00:06:13,672
So Yusuf(يوسُف) stayed in prison for a few more years.

83
00:06:15,362 --> 00:06:18,890
The king, after a few years saw a dream.

84
00:06:21,636 --> 00:06:23,898
We see that dreams are important in their lives.

85
00:06:24,065 --> 00:06:25,385
We have a few dreams here;

86
00:06:25,678 --> 00:06:26,877
a dream of Yaqoob(يعقوب);

87
00:06:27,019 --> 00:06:29,932
a dream of Yusuf(يوسُف);

88
00:06:30,115 --> 00:06:31,218
the dream of the king.

89
00:06:31,329 --> 00:06:33,072
And the dream of these two men in jail.

90
00:06:33,214 --> 00:06:35,627
Dreams played an important role in their lives.

91
00:06:35,778 --> 00:06:41,633
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gives the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) a miracle to challenge the people in the thing that is most important to them.

92
00:06:41,879 --> 00:06:45,943
So Allah has given SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف); the miracle of interpreting dreams.

93
00:06:45,973 --> 00:06:47,038
That's one of his miracles.

94
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:48,562
The King saw dream.

95
00:06:49,030 --> 00:06:57,624
The King saw seven fat cows eaten by seven Ejaaf(عجاف);

96
00:06:57,902 --> 00:07:04,363
Ejaaf(عجاف) means; bones are sticking out, you can see the bone under the flesh, they're very skinny.

97
00:07:05,410 --> 00:07:13,770
So these seven fat cows were eaten up by seven skinny ones; that's one dream.

98
00:07:14,825 --> 00:07:17,511
Either in the same dream or another dream;

99
00:07:17,591 --> 00:07:24,457
he saw seven green ears of corn eaten by seven dry ones.

100
00:07:26,123 --> 00:07:27,234
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

101
00:07:27,425 --> 00:08:01,118
وَقالَ المَلِكُ إِنّي أَرىٰ سَبعَ بَقَراتٍ سِمانٍ يَأكُلُهُنَّ سَبعٌ عِجافٌ وَسَبعَ سُنبُلاتٍ خُضرٍ وَأُخَرَ يابِساتٍ ۖ

102
00:08:01,294 --> 00:08:02,881
And the king of Egypt said;

103
00:08:03,126 --> 00:08:12,170
Verily I saw in a dream seven fat cows, whom seven lean ones were devouring and seven green ears of corn and seven others dry.

104
00:08:12,908 --> 00:08:33,309
يا أَيُّهَا المَلَأُ أَفتوني في رُؤيايَ إِن كُنتُم لِلرُّؤيا تَعبُرونَ۝

105
00:08:33,897 --> 00:08:38,746
Oh notables explained to me my dream if it be that you can interpret dreams.

106
00:08:39,052 --> 00:08:41,808
We have seven fat cows eaten by seven weak ones;

107
00:08:42,139 --> 00:08:46,703
and then seven green ears of corn and seven dry ears of corn.

108
00:08:46,885 --> 00:08:52,754
And then he asked his government and Associates and people please interpret this dream for me.

109
00:08:52,857 --> 00:08:54,913
None of them knew the answer.

110
00:08:55,476 --> 00:08:56,098
They said;

111
00:08:56,375 --> 00:09:16,449
قالوا أَضغاثُ أَحلامٍ ۖ وَما نَحنُ بِتَأويلِ الأَحلامِ بِعالِمينَ۝

112
00:09:16,754 --> 00:09:20,458
Mixed up false dreams, forget about it, this is false dreams, don't worry about it.

113
00:09:21,563 --> 00:09:23,604
وَما نَحنُ بِتَأويلِ الأَحلامِ بِعالِمينَ۝

114
00:09:23,634 --> 00:09:26,658
And we don't have any skill in the interpretation of dreams.

115
00:09:27,436 --> 00:09:29,957
We are not people who care about interpreting dreams.

116
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:34,747
People who are materialistic and attached to life, they don't care about this unseen; Al-Ghaeb(ألغيب)?

117
00:09:35,493 --> 00:09:39,787
The servant was there, the one who was serving the king wine; he was there.

118
00:09:40,199 --> 00:09:43,701
When the topic of dreams was brought up; what did he remember?

119
00:09:44,081 --> 00:09:46,439
He remembered Yusuf(يوسُف) after a few years.

120
00:09:47,209 --> 00:09:48,217
He now remembered.

121
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,560
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

122
00:09:49,772 --> 00:10:14,223
وَقالَ الَّذي نَجا مِنهُما وَادَّكَرَ بَعدَ أُمَّةٍ أَنا أُنَبِّئُكُم بِتَأويلِهِ فَأَرسِلونِ۝

123
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:19,179
Then the man, who was released now at length, remember that said;

124
00:10:19,601 --> 00:10:22,582
I will tell you it's interpretation; so sent me forth.

125
00:10:23,106 --> 00:10:26,415
I will tell you the interpretation let me go and  I'll get you the answer.

126
00:10:26,899 --> 00:10:29,237
So, he went to Sayidina Yusuf عليه السلام and he said;

127
00:10:29,267 --> 00:10:31,531
يوسف أيها الصديق

128
00:10:32,027 --> 00:10:34,298
O Yusuf(يوسُف), man of truth.

129
00:10:35,058 --> 00:10:40,110
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Allah has given the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) the quality of truth and the people know it; Sideeq(ألصديق).

130
00:10:40,558 --> 00:10:42,667
He was called Sideeq(ألصديق) man of truth.

131
00:10:44,014 --> 00:11:18,787
يوسُفُ أَيُّهَا الصِّدّيقُ أَفتِنا في سَبعِ بَقَراتٍ سِمانٍ يَأكُلُهُنَّ سَبعٌ عِجافٌ وَسَبعِ سُنبُلاتٍ خُضرٍ وَأُخَرَ يابِساتٍ

132
00:11:21,969 --> 00:11:40,230
 وَأُخَرَ يابِساتٍ لَعَلّي أَرجِعُ إِلَى النّاسِ لَعَلَّهُم يَعلَمونَ۝

133
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:46,101
Here this man is narrating the dream to SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف);

134
00:11:46,283 --> 00:11:52,977
but Allah is mentioning to us the narration and he's narrating it exactly as the King saw in the dream.

135
00:11:53,763 --> 00:11:55,358
And that is important in dreams.

136
00:11:55,620 --> 00:12:00,594
If you want a dream to be interpreted, it has to be narrated exactly as it was seen?

137
00:12:01,047 --> 00:12:05,586
So here this man is narrating the dream exactly as the King has said it; in the Ayah(آية) before.

138
00:12:06,952 --> 00:12:12,317
Seven fat cows devour by seven weak ones, seven green ears of corn and seven dry ones.

139
00:12:12,547 --> 00:12:15,232
Aftina(أفتنا); tell us the interpretation of this.

140
00:12:15,344 --> 00:12:17,756
So that I can go and let the people know.

141
00:12:18,653 --> 00:12:21,799
Yusuf عليه السّلام now has a bargaining tool in his hand.

142
00:12:21,829 --> 00:12:25,093
He's in jail and this man comes to asking you about the interpretation of the dream.

143
00:12:25,227 --> 00:12:27,515
He could have said: I'm not going to tell you the answer until you free me.

144
00:12:27,785 --> 00:12:30,769
But Yusuf(يوسُف) didn't! He gave him the answer without asking for anything.

145
00:12:32,788 --> 00:12:38,740
He said; and not only did he give the answer, he gave the interpretation and his recommendations.

146
00:12:40,105 --> 00:12:40,702
He said;

147
00:12:40,950 --> 00:13:09,391
قالَ تَزرَعونَ سَبعَ سِنينَ دَأَبًا فَما حَصَدتُم فَذَروهُ في سُنبُلِهِ إِلّا قَليلًا مِمّا تَأكُلونَ۝

148
00:13:09,618 --> 00:13:14,853
For seven consecutive years, you shall, Sow as usual.

149
00:13:15,597 --> 00:13:18,351
For seven years, you're gonna have an abundance of harvest.

150
00:13:18,501 --> 00:13:26,416
These are the seven fat cows, you're gonna have a lot of rain and you're gonna be blessed you're gonna have a lot.

151
00:13:27,249 --> 00:13:28,971
And then he said;

152
00:13:29,186 --> 00:13:33,945
فَما حَصَدتُم فَذَروهُ في سُنبُلِهِ إِلّا قَليلًا مِمّا تَأكُلونَ۝

153
00:13:34,238 --> 00:13:41,737
That harvest which you reap, keep it in the ears except a little of it, which you may eat.

154
00:13:42,332 --> 00:13:48,046
He told them: You need to ration, even though you're gonna have a lot of harvest; Don't use it all.

155
00:13:48,418 --> 00:13:52,913
Save most of it and only use the minimum.

156
00:13:53,659 --> 00:13:56,835
Even though there are years of blessings, don't use it, don't consume it.

157
00:13:57,097 --> 00:14:00,070
Save it all except for what you need for eating.

158
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:05,736
And they used to say, in the Tafseer(تفسير) that SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) would survive on half a meal a day.

159
00:14:06,855 --> 00:14:09,919
And he has ordered the government to ration in the same way.

160
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:12,260
And he would give the example to the people.

161
00:14:12,618 --> 00:14:15,086
He would eat the minimum even though there was an abundance.

162
00:14:15,356 --> 00:14:15,733
Why?

163
00:14:15,763 --> 00:14:18,167
Because he wants them to store the rest.

164
00:14:19,730 --> 00:14:22,730
He told them to keep the grain; the corn in the ear.

165
00:14:23,151 --> 00:14:28,507
There's an interesting story, you know that Sudan is going through an embargo.

166
00:14:30,079 --> 00:14:33,960
Sudani brothers are going through miserable times.

167
00:14:34,730 --> 00:14:42,790
US and its allies are forcing them into this embargo, by this oppressive embargo,

168
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:46,323
and they're not allowing them to export and import.

169
00:14:47,117 --> 00:14:50,490
Sudan has a lot of grain, they have a lot of wheat.

170
00:14:52,814 --> 00:14:59,385
But they're not able to export anything from the outside and they need to store this grain, store it for the future.

171
00:15:00,326 --> 00:15:05,617
But the problem is whenever they would store the grain in this underground bunkers; underground storages.

172
00:15:06,379 --> 00:15:09,873
After a few years it would go bad.

173
00:15:10,087 --> 00:15:18,141
It would spoil because of fungus and humidity and insects and worms and other diseases and bacteria.

174
00:15:18,458 --> 00:15:20,125
So it would spoil it.

175
00:15:20,768 --> 00:15:24,958
They have a lot of wheat, but it would just go bad; it will expire.

176
00:15:26,046 --> 00:15:31,348
There was a Muslim professor who was visiting them; he's a professor in agriculture.

177
00:15:31,839 --> 00:15:33,767
He told them I have a suggestion for you.

178
00:15:34,116 --> 00:15:36,085
Let's try this.

179
00:15:36,759 --> 00:15:41,724
How about instead of storing the grain as seed stored it; in the ears?

180
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:44,303
Let's try with Yusuf عليه السّلام did.

181
00:15:45,050 --> 00:15:46,777
Let's store the grain in the ears.

182
00:15:47,634 --> 00:15:54,707
So they tried it and they stored the grain in the ears and it survived for a much longer period than it was before.

183
00:15:55,919 --> 00:16:01,768
So Yusuf عليه السّلام told them: Keep the grain in the ears; so that we can store it.

184
00:16:03,618 --> 00:16:04,289
And then he said;

185
00:16:04,348 --> 00:16:34,051
ثُمَّ يَأتي مِن بَعدِ ذٰلِكَ سَبعٌ شِدادٌ يَأكُلنَ ما قَدَّمتُم لَهُنَّ إِلّا قَليلًا مِمّا تُحصِنونَ۝

186
00:16:34,378 --> 00:16:38,004
Then we'll come after that 7 hard years

187
00:16:38,296 --> 00:16:44,631
which will devour what you have laid by in advance for them except a little of that which you have guarded stored.

188
00:16:44,981 --> 00:16:50,060
After this seven years of abundance, they would come seven difficult years you would have nothing.

189
00:16:50,766 --> 00:16:53,528
And in those seven years you're going to be eating from what?

190
00:16:53,742 --> 00:16:54,697
From what you have storage.

191
00:16:55,123 --> 00:16:59,627
So these are the seven lean skinny cows eating the seven fat ones.

192
00:17:00,318 --> 00:17:07,696
And the seven green corns, ears of corn, you're going to use them for the seven dry years.

193
00:17:09,204 --> 00:17:11,585
So it gives them recommendation on how to do it.

194
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:17,177
And then he told them something that is not in the dream and this is a wahi(وحي) from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

195
00:17:17,788 --> 00:17:39,101
ثُمَّ يَأتي مِن بَعدِ ذٰلِكَ عامٌ فيهِ يُغاثُ النّاسُ وَفيهِ يَعصِرونَ۝

196
00:17:39,342 --> 00:17:46,413
Then thereafter will come a year in which people will have abundant rain and in which they will press wine and oil.

197
00:17:46,809 --> 00:17:52,826
This is not in the dream but he told them that after the seven difficult years, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will send a lot of rain on you.

198
00:17:55,429 --> 00:17:57,014
This was conveyed to the king.

199
00:17:59,009 --> 00:18:05,334
The king was impressed He wanted to make use of this expertise.

200
00:18:05,884 --> 00:18:12,035
وَقالَ المَلِكُ ائتوني بِهِ ۖ

201
00:18:12,313 --> 00:18:15,519
The king said: Bring him forth; Bring him to me.

202
00:18:16,091 --> 00:18:18,806
The messenger went to convey this news to SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف);

203
00:18:18,866 --> 00:18:25,244
he told them the king is offering you to leave prison and jail, you're free, you're free to leave.

204
00:18:25,569 --> 00:18:30,918
Not only are you free to leave, but the king wants to have you as one of his advisors.

205
00:18:33,232 --> 00:18:34,169
Look at this honor;

206
00:18:34,605 --> 00:18:39,612
Not only is he gonna leave jail after years, but he's gonna be an advisor of the king.

207
00:18:41,072 --> 00:18:43,684
But the response of Yusuf عليه السّلام was amazing.

208
00:18:44,096 --> 00:18:46,747
It was even amazing to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

209
00:18:47,303 --> 00:18:48,797
Yusuf(يوسُف) said: No, I'm not gonna leave;

210
00:18:49,948 --> 00:18:53,242
You're offered to leave jail, here the doors are open; leave.

211
00:18:53,781 --> 00:18:56,216
And you can be an advisor for the king.

212
00:18:56,246 --> 00:18:57,432
He said: I'm not gonna leave.

213
00:18:58,361 --> 00:18:59,512
SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) said;

214
00:18:59,718 --> 00:19:26,186
فَلَمّا جاءَهُ الرَّسولُ قالَ ارجِع إِلىٰ رَبِّكَ فَاسأَلهُ ما بالُ النِّسوَةِ اللّاتي قَطَّعنَ أَيدِيَهُنَّ ۚ

215
00:19:26,645 --> 00:19:31,714
Return to your Lord and ask him what happened to the woman who cut their hands.

216
00:19:32,714 --> 00:19:35,754
Surely my Lord; Allah is well aware of their plot.

217
00:19:36,476 --> 00:19:41,741
Yusuf عليه السّلام did not want to leave prison until his innocence is established.

218
00:19:42,868 --> 00:19:46,416
Because he was put in jail and he's innocent.

219
00:19:47,241 --> 00:19:52,394
And he does not want to leave jail as a favor given to him by the king.

220
00:19:52,424 --> 00:19:55,457
No! He wants to leave jail with everybody knowing that he's innocent.

221
00:19:56,203 --> 00:19:57,552
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

222
00:19:57,679 --> 00:20:02,966
رحم الله يوسف لو كنت أنا لبعدرت الباب او لعجبت الداعي

223
00:20:03,133 --> 00:20:04,321
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

224
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:10,720
May Allah have mercy on Yusuf(يوسُف); if it was me, I would have rushed towards the door and responded to the call.

225
00:20:11,343 --> 00:20:15,683
Staying in, years for years; staying in prison for years, and then you're offered to leave

226
00:20:15,743 --> 00:20:19,778
and you say: No, I'm not gonna leave; Until my innocence is established.

227
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:27,182
 But the story of Yusuf(يوسُف) is an example from the beginning to the end; It's an example of patience, Sabr(صبر).

228
00:20:27,659 --> 00:20:29,768
That is the essence of the story of Yusuf(يوسُف).

229
00:20:31,514 --> 00:20:36,260
Go and ask the king, what is the story of the woman who cut their hands?

230
00:20:36,768 --> 00:20:39,092
So he wants his case to be open again.

231
00:20:40,207 --> 00:20:43,413
So the king investigated in this case.

232
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:48,730
And then he brought these women and he asked them this question.

233
00:20:48,952 --> 00:21:01,415
قالَ ما خَطبُكُنَّ إِذ راوَدتُنَّ يوسُفَ عَن نَفسِهِ ۚ

234
00:21:01,796 --> 00:21:07,423
The king said to the women, what was your affair when you did seek to seduce Yusuf(يوسُف)?

235
00:21:08,486 --> 00:21:09,688
The women told the truth,

236
00:21:10,036 --> 00:21:13,441
قُلنَ حاشَ لِلَّهِ ما عَلِمنا عَلَيهِ مِن سوءٍ ۚ

237
00:21:13,822 --> 00:21:17,520
The women said; Allah forbid no evil, know we against him.

238
00:21:18,324 --> 00:21:21,904
All of these women witness the truth and said;

239
00:21:22,324 --> 00:21:25,920
Yusuf(يوسُف) is innocent, and he has committed no evil.

240
00:21:27,415 --> 00:21:33,820
At that particular moment, the wife of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز), when she saw that the case is exposed and the truth is known.

241
00:21:33,978 --> 00:21:34,396
She said;

242
00:21:34,426 --> 00:22:01,013
قالَتِ امرَأَتُ العَزيزِ الآنَ حَصحَصَ الحَقُّ أَنا راوَدتُهُ عَن نَفسِهِ وَإِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الصّادِقينَ۝

243
00:22:01,609 --> 00:22:02,664
She said;

244
00:22:03,053 --> 00:22:08,424
 Now the truth is manifest to all and she admitted her guilt and said;

245
00:22:08,646 --> 00:22:12,101
أَنا راوَدتُهُ عَن نَفسِهِ وَإِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الصّادِقينَ۝

246
00:22:12,299 --> 00:22:17,148
It was I who sought to seduce him and he is surely of the truthful.

247
00:22:18,378 --> 00:22:21,993
Now the innocence of Yusuf(يوسُف) is established, and then she said;

248
00:22:22,223 --> 00:22:45,423
ذٰلِكَ لِيَعلَمَ أَنّي لَم أَخُنهُ بِالغَيبِ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَهدي كَيدَ الخائِنينَ۝

249
00:22:45,761 --> 00:22:47,118
Then Yusuf(يوسُف) said;

250
00:22:47,221 --> 00:22:54,528
I asked for this inquiry in an order that he Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) may know that I betrayed him not in secret;

251
00:22:54,703 --> 00:22:57,346
and verily Allah guides not the plot of the betrayal.

252
00:22:57,376 --> 00:23:01,568
So here in the translation, they believe that these are words of Yusuf(يوسُف).

253
00:23:01,598 --> 00:23:04,576
There's a difference of opinion, whether it's the words of Yusuf(يوسُف) or her words.

254
00:23:04,759 --> 00:23:06,917
If it's the words of Yusuf(يوسُف) he is saying;

255
00:23:07,417 --> 00:23:11,105
Because who was the Sayyid(سيد) of Yusuf(يوسُف) - who was a slave owner?

256
00:23:11,155 --> 00:23:13,437
It was the husband of this woman.

257
00:23:13,917 --> 00:23:19,934
So Yusuf(يوسُف) after she admitted, he said, this is so that my Lord would know that I'm innocent.

258
00:23:20,664 --> 00:23:22,606
And this is her husband.

259
00:23:22,862 --> 00:23:26,192
And it's not me who tried to seduce her, it is her.

260
00:23:27,001 --> 00:23:33,543
And I free not myself from the blame, verily the human self is inclined to evil

261
00:23:33,669 --> 00:23:39,822
except when my lord bestows His mercy upon whom He wills verily my lord is aft forgiving, Most Merciful.

262
00:23:40,306 --> 00:23:41,304
Now the king said;

263
00:23:41,377 --> 00:23:54,259
وَقالَ المَلِكُ ائتوني بِهِ أَستَخلِصهُ لِنَفسي ۖ

264
00:23:55,002 --> 00:23:59,060
And the king said: Bring him to me that I may attach him to my person.

265
00:23:59,282 --> 00:24:06,329
So they brought Saydina Yusuf عليه السّلام honored out of jail with his innocence established and now he is with the king.

266
00:24:06,789 --> 00:24:08,043
And he talked with the king.

267
00:24:08,409 --> 00:24:11,533
The king was even more impressed with him, when he talked to him.

268
00:24:12,207 --> 00:24:13,549
After he talked with him.

269
00:24:13,834 --> 00:24:30,730
فَلَمّا كَلَّمَهُ قالَ إِنَّكَ اليَومَ لَدَينا مَكينٌ أَمينٌ۝

270
00:24:31,373 --> 00:24:33,013
Then when he spoke to him, he said;

271
00:24:33,103 --> 00:24:37,341
Verily this day, you are with us high in rank and fully trusted.

272
00:24:37,745 --> 00:24:41,253
Now I trust you fully, and now I would give you authority.

273
00:24:41,928 --> 00:24:44,762
In that moment in the SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) said;

274
00:24:45,603 --> 00:25:02,178
قالَ اجعَلني عَلىٰ خَزائِنِ الأَرضِ ۖ إِنّي حَفيظٌ عَليمٌ۝

275
00:25:02,757 --> 00:25:03,646
He said;

276
00:25:04,535 --> 00:25:08,075
Set me over the store houses of the land.

277
00:25:08,678 --> 00:25:11,835
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Yusuf(يوسُف) is asking for position.

278
00:25:14,041 --> 00:25:19,023
We know that in Islam, we're not supposed to ask for a position of leadership.

279
00:25:19,816 --> 00:25:20,691
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

280
00:25:20,721 --> 00:25:23,919
إنَّا وَاللَّهِ لا نُوَلِّي علَى هذا العَمَلِ أَحَدًا سَأَلَهُ،

281
00:25:24,229 --> 00:25:27,905
We do not appoint to the position of leadership; whoever asks for it.

282
00:25:28,564 --> 00:25:32,619
If you are seeking the position of leadership, you should not be given that position;

283
00:25:33,254 --> 00:25:35,355
But SaydinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) is asking for that position.

284
00:25:36,196 --> 00:25:39,982
And then SaydinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) is doing something else that we don't do in Islam, he said;

285
00:25:40,799 --> 00:25:42,505
إِنّي حَفيظٌ عَليمٌ۝

286
00:25:43,311 --> 00:25:50,026
I am Hafeez(حفيظ) meaning I will protect it and Aleem(عليم) I'm knowledgeable.

287
00:25:51,026 --> 00:25:51,937
And in Islam we know,

288
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:53,298
ولا تزكو أنفسكم

289
00:25:53,328 --> 00:25:54,628
Do not praise yourselves.

290
00:25:55,960 --> 00:26:00,110
Allah tells us in Qur'an don’t praise yourself don’t give yourself credit and praise yourself.

291
00:26:00,404 --> 00:26:03,150
And Yusuf(يوسُف) is giving himself praise.

292
00:26:03,428 --> 00:26:04,201
He saying;

293
00:26:04,420 --> 00:26:06,112
أنا حفيظ و عليم

294
00:26:06,301 --> 00:26:10,004
I will protect it, I have the ability to protect and take care of it.

295
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:11,827
And Aleem(عليم); I'm knowledgeable.

296
00:26:15,430 --> 00:26:18,399
The scholars say that

297
00:26:19,693 --> 00:26:25,025
when you are the only person who is able to take that position, then you're allowed to ask for it.

298
00:26:27,007 --> 00:26:30,150
And Yusuf(يوسُف) was the only one, who was fit for that position.

299
00:26:30,888 --> 00:26:35,485
If he left it, it would have been taken by somebody who will not take care of it.

300
00:26:38,699 --> 00:26:46,850
Number two, if you are not well known to the people, then you are allowed to introduce yourself.

301
00:26:49,667 --> 00:26:54,437
In the Islamic community, when everybody around you is Muslim;

302
00:26:55,079 --> 00:26:59,676
you should not go and ask for a position of leadership and authority because everyone around you is Muslim.

303
00:27:00,795 --> 00:27:05,125
And when you are part of the community and people know you should not go and praise yourself.

304
00:27:06,157 --> 00:27:10,800
But Yusuf عليه السّلام is not known; They don't know him yet he just came out of jail.

305
00:27:10,998 --> 00:27:12,997
So he need to tell them his credentials.

306
00:27:14,067 --> 00:27:18,497
And also he's the only one who knows what's going on and knows this future.

307
00:27:18,759 --> 00:27:23,451
Therefore, if he leaves it, that will be an irresponsible stance,

308
00:27:23,481 --> 00:27:27,752
because it will be taken by somebody who will corrupt and will not be able to take this authority.

309
00:27:28,284 --> 00:27:31,749
So this is why SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) asked for that position of leadership

310
00:27:31,983 --> 00:27:34,793
and that's why he told them about himself

311
00:27:35,269 --> 00:27:41,165
and Yusuf عليه السّلام was not asking this position for fame, or power.

312
00:27:41,475 --> 00:27:48,151
No, he knew from the beginning, that he will be taken care of Egypt in one of its most difficult times.

313
00:27:48,730 --> 00:27:51,452
Who wants to take care of a government that is broke.

314
00:27:52,516 --> 00:27:56,278
He's gonna take care of Egypt in seven of the most devastating years,

315
00:27:56,794 --> 00:27:58,580
years of hunger and famine.

316
00:27:59,587 --> 00:28:04,478
Prime Ministers run away from positions like this because this is the end of your career.

317
00:28:05,017 --> 00:28:08,613
If a stock market crash happens in your time you lost your job.

318
00:28:09,192 --> 00:28:13,302
And we know it that whole governments would collapse because of this.

319
00:28:13,691 --> 00:28:17,762
So there's no honor and taking that position, it's a very difficult and critical moment.

320
00:28:18,127 --> 00:28:22,836
But Yusuf(يوسُف) wants to take that position, not for the honor and the prestige and the fame of it;

321
00:28:22,979 --> 00:28:26,901
No! He's doing it as a service to take care of the people of Egypt.

322
00:28:27,662 --> 00:28:46,049
وَكَذٰلِكَ مَكَّنّا لِيوسُفَ فِي الأَرضِ يَتَبَوَّأُ مِنها حَيثُ يَشاءُ ۚ

323
00:28:48,025 --> 00:29:05,000
نُصيبُ بِرَحمَتِنا مَن نَشاءُ ۖ وَلا نُضيعُ أَجرَ المُحسِنينَ۝

324
00:29:05,567 --> 00:29:08,722
Thus do we give full authority to Yusuf(يوسُف) in the land?

325
00:29:09,008 --> 00:29:13,483
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى now has established Yusuf(يوسُف) firmly in the land.

326
00:29:13,785 --> 00:29:15,230
يَتَبَوَّأُ مِنها حَيثُ يَشاءُ ۚ

327
00:29:15,260 --> 00:29:17,459
He will go wherever he wants with authority.

328
00:29:18,086 --> 00:29:21,567
It is said that the king told him; Do whatever you want in the kingdom.

329
00:29:21,964 --> 00:29:27,612
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says that Yusuf(يوسُف) can go anywhere in Egypt and he has full authority to do whatever he wants.

330
00:29:28,231 --> 00:29:35,747
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى established SaydinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) who was sold as a slave, who faced death.

331
00:29:36,145 --> 00:29:39,312
Now Yusuf(يوسُف) became the most powerful person in Egypt.

332
00:29:39,621 --> 00:29:43,201
He had the Treasury he had the authority all under his hands.

333
00:29:43,904 --> 00:29:45,626
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

334
00:29:45,800 --> 00:30:01,938
وَلَأَجرُ الآخِرَةِ خَيرٌ لِلَّذينَ آمَنوا وَكانوا يَتَّقونَ۝

335
00:30:02,033 --> 00:30:08,252
And verily the reward of the Hereafter is better for those who believe and use to be obedient to Allah.

336
00:30:08,752 --> 00:30:11,675
Allah is telling us so that we don't think that Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is something worthy;

337
00:30:11,950 --> 00:30:16,066
Allah is telling us that the reward of Yusuf(يوسُف) in Akhirah(آخرة) is the true reward.

338
00:30:16,293 --> 00:30:20,754
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is saving the reward for Yusuf(يوسُف) in Akhirah(آخرة) that is the place of reward.

339
00:30:21,222 --> 00:30:28,859
The famine that striked Egypt wasn't limited to that area.

340
00:30:30,193 --> 00:30:34,879
It had some effects on the surrounding areas, including Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

341
00:30:36,339 --> 00:30:42,252
So this drought not only affected the area of Egypt,

342
00:30:43,006 --> 00:30:50,137
but also over spilled to the areas of Falistine(فلسطين) and Syria and those parts of the world.

343
00:30:51,486 --> 00:30:56,671
So the place where Yaqoob عليه السّلام was living, was suffering from that drought.

344
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:03,787
But now all the people are Egypt have nothing to eat;

345
00:31:04,470 --> 00:31:09,002
because they don't have someone like Yusuf(يوسُف) to manage their affairs.

346
00:31:10,279 --> 00:31:15,973
So everyone was running out of wealth and money and food, except Egypt.

347
00:31:16,552 --> 00:31:21,490
Egypt had enough to feed the people of Egypt and to feed its neighbors

348
00:31:21,692 --> 00:31:24,326
because of the wonderful management of SaydinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

349
00:31:25,776 --> 00:31:33,249
So now the brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف) are going to the center of the drought, the famine; Egypt to ask for food.

350
00:31:33,697 --> 00:31:37,403
Even though that is where the center of the drought and the famine is;

351
00:31:37,547 --> 00:31:39,784
but that is where everybody's going to ask for food.

352
00:31:40,037 --> 00:31:40,441
Why?

353
00:31:40,471 --> 00:31:46,125
Because it was under a just and great manager and that Saydina Yusuf عليه السّلام.

354
00:31:46,558 --> 00:31:49,405
So sometimes it's not a matter of how much wealth the earth has;

355
00:31:49,643 --> 00:31:56,294
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will put blessing, even if there is dry, if there is Adl(عدل); if there is justice.

356
00:31:57,453 --> 00:32:02,779
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says: Justice is the think that the heavens and Earth are established on.

357
00:32:03,001 --> 00:32:05,713
Whenever it is missing, everything will go corrupt.

358
00:32:06,706 --> 00:32:14,570
There is under you could be filled with wealth; Oil could be pumping out of the ground.

359
00:32:16,126 --> 00:32:18,602
Harvest could be filling your storages.

360
00:32:18,912 --> 00:32:21,883
Nevertheless, you would have poverty in the streets.

361
00:32:22,367 --> 00:32:24,074
Why? Because justice is missing.

362
00:32:24,693 --> 00:32:30,263
But you could have a land that is completely dry and drought and there's nothing growing up; like in Egypt.

363
00:32:30,700 --> 00:32:33,343
Nevertheless, everybody's going to Egypt to get their ration.

364
00:32:35,438 --> 00:32:39,277
So it's not a matter of how much your earth is producing; It's a matter of the Justice; Al-Adl(ألعدل).

365
00:32:40,197 --> 00:32:42,832
In the time of Imam Ahmad Ibn Hanbal(إمام أحمد إبن حنبل);

366
00:32:43,356 --> 00:32:47,623
Imam Ahmad Ibn Hanbal(إمام أحمد إبن حنبل) said: We were opening up some of the storages of Bani Ummayah(بني أميَّة).

367
00:32:48,218 --> 00:32:52,099
Bani Ummayah(بني أميَّة) are the ruling family of the Muslim world for a few decades.

368
00:32:53,432 --> 00:32:56,238
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) said: We were opening some of their storages;

369
00:32:56,659 --> 00:33:03,602
So we found the sack and in the sack we found a mustard seed.

370
00:33:03,673 --> 00:33:05,768
Now the mustard seed is very, very small.

371
00:33:06,133 --> 00:33:08,006
It's very small seed; very small.

372
00:33:08,546 --> 00:33:11,689
But this mustard seed like was the seed of a date.

373
00:33:12,348 --> 00:33:16,794
The size of the mustard seed was like a seed of a date; this big.

374
00:33:17,350 --> 00:33:21,796
And that seed was put in this small sack written on it was;

375
00:33:22,145 --> 00:33:28,325
This used to grow in the time of justice; the time of Umar Ibn Abdelaziz(عمر إبن عبدالعزيز).

376
00:33:30,301 --> 00:33:36,694
This type of Mustard seed used to grow, in the time of justice in the time of Umar Ibn Abdelaziz(عمر إبن عبدالعزيز).

377
00:33:37,186 --> 00:33:41,552
So Allah blesses even the land because of the justice of the ruler.

378
00:33:42,314 --> 00:33:43,441
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

379
00:33:43,560 --> 00:34:02,823
وَجاءَ إِخوَةُ يوسُفَ فَدَخَلوا عَلَيهِ فَعَرَفَهُم وَهُم لَهُ مُنكِرونَ۝

380
00:34:03,213 --> 00:34:09,656
And Yusuf(يوسُف) bretherin came and they entered into him and he recognized them but they did not recognize him.

381
00:34:09,823 --> 00:34:10,466
He knew them;

382
00:34:10,926 --> 00:34:13,188
He knew that these are my brothers but they didn't know him.

383
00:34:15,475 --> 00:34:16,022
They came;

384
00:34:16,052 --> 00:34:17,122
Why did they come to Egypt?

385
00:34:17,578 --> 00:34:20,649
To receive ration; some food.

386
00:34:22,118 --> 00:34:23,391
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

387
00:34:24,436 --> 00:34:42,540
وَلَمّا جَهَّزَهُم بِجَهازِهِم قالَ ائتوني بِأَخٍ لَكُم مِن أَبيكُم ۚ

388
00:34:45,405 --> 00:35:01,190
أَلا تَرَونَ أَنّي أوفِي الكَيلَ وَأَنا خَيرُ المُنزِلينَ۝

389
00:35:01,886 --> 00:35:04,557
Yusuf(يوسُف) use to give ration per head.

390
00:35:05,238 --> 00:35:08,807
So he would give every individual a camel load.

391
00:35:09,331 --> 00:35:11,085
So how many brothers were these?

392
00:35:11,767 --> 00:35:13,764
There were ten brothers.

393
00:35:13,958 --> 00:35:16,035
So he gave them 10 camel loads.

394
00:35:16,392 --> 00:35:17,489
And then he was talking to them.

395
00:35:17,519 --> 00:35:19,408
He told them, how many brothers are you?

396
00:35:19,598 --> 00:35:20,585
They said: We're eleven.

397
00:35:20,741 --> 00:35:23,064
He said: Why didn't you bring the 11th brother with you?

398
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:24,531
They said: He's with his father.

399
00:35:24,857 --> 00:35:27,254
He said: Okay, next you bring him with you.

400
00:35:27,563 --> 00:35:30,393
Because as you see, I will give you a full load per head.

401
00:35:30,528 --> 00:35:34,298
If you bring him with you, instead of going back home with 10 loads, you'll get 11.

402
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:35,467
This is Targheeb(ترغيب).

403
00:35:35,753 --> 00:35:37,547
He's trying to encourage them to bring their brother

404
00:35:37,777 --> 00:35:39,742
and then he is using Tarheeb(ترهيب); threatening them.

405
00:35:40,047 --> 00:35:42,610
And if you don't bring him with you, I'm not gonna give you anything.

406
00:35:43,269 --> 00:35:44,891
So he's using Targheeb(ترغيب) and Tarheeb(ترهيب);

407
00:35:45,510 --> 00:35:46,740
The carrot and the stick.

408
00:35:47,113 --> 00:35:50,311
The carrot, bring your brother I'll give you 11 loads.

409
00:35:51,192 --> 00:35:53,699
The stick if you don't bring him or you're gonna get zero; nothing.

410
00:35:54,056 --> 00:36:10,219
فَإِن لَم تَأتوني بِهِ فَلا كَيلَ لَكُم عِندي وَلا تَقرَبونِ۝

411
00:36:10,405 --> 00:36:16,338
But if you bring him not; there shall be no measure of corn for you with me, nor shall you even come near me.

412
00:36:18,129 --> 00:36:18,708
They said;

413
00:36:18,788 --> 00:36:32,936
قالوا سَنُراوِدُ عَنهُ أَباهُ وَإِنّا لَفاعِلونَ۝

414
00:36:33,325 --> 00:36:38,384
They said: We shall try to get permission for him from his father and verily we shall do it.

415
00:36:39,495 --> 00:36:44,798
The brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف) of they brought with them some merchandise; to do trade.

416
00:36:45,219 --> 00:36:50,512
So they gave this stuff that they brought with them and they took instead of it; food.

417
00:36:51,593 --> 00:36:57,061
The merchandise that they brought was worthless; really it wasn't very valuable.

418
00:36:58,109 --> 00:37:02,612
Saydina Yusuf عليه السّلام said;

419
00:37:03,342 --> 00:37:08,221
Go and put it back in their luggage.

420
00:37:09,046 --> 00:37:14,427
This merchandise that they brought; Put it back in their luggage without them knowing.

421
00:37:14,737 --> 00:37:16,234
Why did SaydinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) do that.?

422
00:37:17,152 --> 00:37:23,612
So that when they go back home they would have something to bring next year with them to do trade.

423
00:37:24,628 --> 00:37:30,165
Yusuf(يوسُف) was afraid that maybe they would go home and they would have nothing left to bring with them next year.

424
00:37:30,625 --> 00:37:34,913
So they would think; well if we don't have anything to give, how can we take corn.

425
00:37:35,096 --> 00:37:36,000
So, Yusuf(يوسُف) said;

426
00:37:36,088 --> 00:37:39,683
Give them back what they brought so that they will use it to come back next year.

427
00:37:39,857 --> 00:37:44,588
Yusuf(يوسُف) told his servants to put their money which they have brought with them into their bags;

428
00:37:44,731 --> 00:37:49,088
so that they might know it when they go back to their people in order that they may come back.

429
00:37:49,691 --> 00:38:10,836
فَلَمّا رَجَعوا إِلىٰ أَبيهِم قالوا يا أَبانا مُنِعَ مِنَّا الكَيلُ

430
00:38:13,431 --> 00:38:40,665
 قالوا يا أَبانا مُنِعَ مِنَّا الكَيلُ فَأَرسِل مَعَنا أَخانا نَكتَل وَإِنّا لَهُ لَحافِظونَ۝

431
00:38:41,269 --> 00:38:43,060
When they went back to their father, they said;

432
00:38:43,090 --> 00:38:47,867
Oh our father, no more measure of grain will be given to us unless we take our brother;

433
00:38:47,963 --> 00:38:52,463
so send our brother with us and we shall get our measure and truly we will guard him.

434
00:38:52,677 --> 00:38:53,487
Who was this brother?

435
00:38:53,517 --> 00:38:58,210
This was Binyameen(بنيامين); the brother of Yusuf(يوسُف) from the same mother.

436
00:38:59,694 --> 00:39:05,704
Sayidina Yaqub عليه السلام was protective of Binyameen(بنيامين) just like he was with Yusuf(يوسُف).

437
00:39:06,497 --> 00:39:10,164
And he would not trust his brothers to take care of him.

438
00:39:12,355 --> 00:39:14,760
So the brothers are trying to convince the father they said;

439
00:39:14,790 --> 00:39:17,966
Listen; If you don't send them we can't give anything's.

440
00:39:19,942 --> 00:39:24,556
Yaqoob(يعقوب) knows what they have done with Yusuf(يوسُف); that they have made a conspiracy against him.

441
00:39:24,586 --> 00:39:26,914
 He doesn't want this to happen with Binyameen(بنيامين) again.

442
00:39:28,398 --> 00:39:47,315
قالَ هَل آمَنُكُم عَلَيهِ إِلّا كَما أَمِنتُكُم عَلىٰ أَخيهِ مِن قَبلُ ۖ

443
00:39:50,353 --> 00:40:02,855
فَاللَّهُ خَيرٌ حافِظًا ۖ وَهُوَ أَرحَمُ الرّاحِمينَ۝

444
00:40:03,495 --> 00:40:09,153
He said: Can I entrust him, to you except as I entrust his brother Yusuf(يوسُف) to you afore time;

445
00:40:09,565 --> 00:40:13,950
but Allah is the best to guard and He is the most Merciful of those who show mercy.

446
00:40:15,196 --> 00:40:29,828
وَلَمّا فَتَحوا مَتاعَهُم وَجَدوا بِضاعَتَهُم رُدَّت إِلَيهِم ۖ

447
00:40:32,606 --> 00:40:49,884
قالوا يا أَبانا ما نَبغي ۖ هٰذِهِ بِضاعَتُنا رُدَّت إِلَينا ۖ

448
00:40:52,178 --> 00:41:21,780
هٰذِهِ بِضاعَتُنا رُدَّت إِلَينا ۖ وَنَميرُ أَهلَنا وَنَحفَظُ أَخانا وَنَزدادُ كَيلَ بَعيرٍ ۖ ذٰلِكَ كَيلٌ يَسيرٌ۝

449
00:41:22,364 --> 00:41:26,189
And when they opened their bags they found their money had been returned to them.

450
00:41:26,249 --> 00:41:29,233
They said: Oh our Father, what more can we desire?

451
00:41:29,301 --> 00:41:31,793
This is our money it has been returned to us.

452
00:41:32,039 --> 00:41:34,458
So we shall get more food for our family.

453
00:41:34,643 --> 00:41:39,017
And we shall guard our brother and add one more measure of a camel's load;

454
00:41:39,263 --> 00:41:42,001
This quantity is easy for the king to give.

455
00:41:43,297 --> 00:41:46,519
Now, Yaqoob(يعقوب) is almost convinced, but he said;

456
00:41:46,806 --> 00:42:12,846
قالَ لَن أُرسِلَهُ مَعَكُم حَتّىٰ تُؤتونِ مَوثِقًا مِنَ اللَّهِ لَتَأتُنَّني بِهِ إِلّا أَن يُحاطَ بِكُم ۖ

457
00:42:13,128 --> 00:42:17,538
I'm not going to send him with you; Unless You promise me

458
00:42:17,887 --> 00:42:24,886
that you will not forsake him unless you are surrounded, and there's no way for you to survive.

459
00:42:25,418 --> 00:42:28,249
Don't come to me alive without Binyameen(بنيامين).

460
00:42:30,154 --> 00:42:32,265
And I want you to give me your promise.

461
00:42:34,844 --> 00:42:37,971
He; Jacob said: I will not send them with you;

462
00:42:38,186 --> 00:42:46,862
until you swear an oath to me in Allah's name, that you will bring him back to me unless you all, yourself surrounded.

463
00:42:47,354 --> 00:42:51,229
So they gave him the promise and when they had sworn their solemn oath, he said;

464
00:42:51,346 --> 00:42:54,394
Allah is the witness over that which you said.

465
00:42:55,539 --> 00:42:59,746
These 11 brothers were strong and handsome.

466
00:43:00,373 --> 00:43:08,761
And I mean you have 11 sons; That is something that people are going to be jealous about.

467
00:43:09,943 --> 00:43:15,485
Sayidina Yaqub(سيدنا يعقوب) might have been worried of the effect of the evil eye; Al-Ain(ألعين).

468
00:43:15,586 --> 00:43:17,230
And this is Haqq(حَقّ). Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

469
00:43:17,260 --> 00:43:17,778
  ألعين حقَ

470
00:43:17,865 --> 00:43:19,230
The evil eye is true.

471
00:43:20,325 --> 00:43:26,612
The evil eye is some ability that some people have to cause you harm when they are jealous of you.

472
00:43:29,064 --> 00:43:30,445
So Sayidina Yaqub(سيدنا يعقوب) said;

473
00:43:30,778 --> 00:43:51,129
وَقالَ يا بَنِيَّ لا تَدخُلوا مِن بابٍ واحِدٍ وَادخُلوا مِن أَبوابٍ مُتَفَرِّقَةٍ ۖ

474
00:43:51,430 --> 00:43:56,256
And he said: Oh my sons do not enter by one gate, but enter by different gates.

475
00:43:56,430 --> 00:44:00,222
Don't go all of you together from one gate, go from different gates,

476
00:44:00,452 --> 00:44:03,126
because if you go all of you together, people will be jealous.

477
00:44:03,388 --> 00:44:07,076
So break up into groups and go from different gates.

478
00:44:07,989 --> 00:44:13,046
Yaqoob(يعقوب) is telling them this, to keep them away from the evil eye;

479
00:44:13,363 --> 00:44:16,688
but then Yaqoob(يعقوب) is clarifying something; He said;

480
00:44:17,125 --> 00:44:28,915
وَما أُغني عَنكُم مِنَ اللَّهِ مِن شَيءٍ ۖ

481
00:44:29,804 --> 00:44:32,534
And I can't avail you against Allah at all;

482
00:44:32,867 --> 00:44:38,599
this is means that you could follow; this is a Sabab(سبب) but it is not this; that could save you; It is Allah.

483
00:44:39,057 --> 00:44:43,986
So we follow the means, but then we leave the matter in the hands of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; that Twakul(توكل).

484
00:44:45,097 --> 00:44:52,208
إِنِ الحُكمُ إِلّا لِلَّهِ ۖ

485
00:44:52,605 --> 00:44:55,540
Allah Ho Akbar(ألله أكبر) even Yaqoob(يعقوب) is emphasizing in this again and he is saying;

486
00:44:55,570 --> 00:44:56,899
إِنِ الحُكمُ إِلّا لِلَّهِ ۖ

487
00:44:56,963 --> 00:45:01,971
The command and the decision, rests only with Allah.

488
00:45:02,583 --> 00:45:03,472
And then he said;

489
00:45:03,742 --> 00:45:18,138
عَلَيهِ تَوَكَّلتُ ۖ وَعَلَيهِ فَليَتَوَكَّلِ المُتَوَكِّلونَ۝

490
00:45:18,590 --> 00:45:23,794
In Him I put my trust and let all those that trust put their trust in Allah.

491
00:45:24,334 --> 00:45:46,513
وَلَمّا دَخَلوا مِن حَيثُ أَمَرَهُم أَبوهُم ما كانَ يُغني عَنهُم مِنَ اللَّهِ مِن شَيءٍ

492
00:45:49,203 --> 00:46:00,064
إِلّا حاجَةً في نَفسِ يَعقوبَ قَضاها ۚ

493
00:46:00,646 --> 00:46:04,408
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says and when they entered according to their father's advice;

494
00:46:04,662 --> 00:46:08,519
It did not avail them in the least; against the will of Allah.

495
00:46:08,741 --> 00:46:12,873
It was but a need of Jacob's inner self which he discharged.

496
00:46:13,286 --> 00:46:17,151
It is not this that will save them; It is the will of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

497
00:46:19,908 --> 00:46:24,797
So they entered and met with Sayidina Yusuf عليه السّلام.

498
00:46:25,718 --> 00:46:27,857
When they came in to meet Yusuf(يوسُف);

499
00:46:29,912 --> 00:46:35,612
Yusuf عليه السّلام took Binyamin(بنيامين) to the side without the brothers knowing

500
00:46:37,498 --> 00:46:41,824
and he told him Binyamin(بنيامين); Do you know who's speaking to you?

501
00:46:42,784 --> 00:46:44,225
This is your brother Yusuf(يوسُف).

502
00:46:45,391 --> 00:46:50,262
He embraced his brother and hugged him and he told him;

503
00:46:51,881 --> 00:47:08,637
قالَ إِنّي أَنا أَخوكَ فَلا تَبتَئِس بِما كانوا يَعمَلونَ۝

504
00:47:08,951 --> 00:47:14,208
Verily, I am your brother so grieved not for what they used to do.

505
00:47:15,597 --> 00:47:17,311
And then SayidinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) made a plan.

506
00:47:18,605 --> 00:47:25,070
SayidinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) provided them with their camel loads; 11 camel loads.

507
00:47:26,443 --> 00:47:35,444
And then he took Suwaa Malik(صواع ملك), the cup of the king, which was made of gold, very valuable thing that belonged to the king.

508
00:47:36,822 --> 00:47:42,719
And he put it in the luggage of his brother Binyamin(بنيامين).

509
00:47:44,052 --> 00:47:46,736
He sticks it in there without nobody knowing.

510
00:47:48,268 --> 00:47:51,371
All of the brothers, they loaded all of their luggage and they started to leave.

511
00:47:51,871 --> 00:47:53,907
And suddenly they heard that announcement.

512
00:47:54,399 --> 00:48:11,317
ثُمَّ أَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ أَيَّتُهَا العيرُ إِنَّكُم لَسارِقونَ۝

513
00:48:11,554 --> 00:48:15,364
That the cup of the king has been stolen.

514
00:48:17,197 --> 00:48:20,214
So they said: We did not come to cause corruption in the land;

515
00:48:20,244 --> 00:48:23,285
This is not our habit or custom;

516
00:48:23,315 --> 00:48:25,222
We're not robbers, we're not thieves.

517
00:48:26,190 --> 00:48:27,199
They said;

518
00:48:29,080 --> 00:48:32,811
If you are not thieves, we have to look at your luggage we're going to look in every luggage

519
00:48:32,841 --> 00:48:35,938
but what if we find that in your luggage what will happen?

520
00:48:37,192 --> 00:48:46,936
They said: If you find this; in our luggage, then you take the guilty one as a slave with you.

521
00:48:48,365 --> 00:48:50,825
This used to be the law of Yaqoob(يعقوب).

522
00:48:51,960 --> 00:48:59,680
The law of Sayidina Yaqub(سيدنا يعقوب) is that whoever steals is captured as a prisoner by the owner of the goods.

523
00:49:01,220 --> 00:49:08,209
The law of the king of Egypt, whom Yusuf(يوسُف) is working under Is that

524
00:49:08,239 --> 00:49:11,614
the one who steals is punished; the certain punishment.

525
00:49:12,749 --> 00:49:15,217
Yusuf(يوسُف) does not want his brother to be punished.

526
00:49:16,169 --> 00:49:18,085
Yusuf(يوسُف) wants to take his brother.

527
00:49:18,633 --> 00:49:25,404
So Yusuf(يوسُف) made trick; this plan to take his brother according to their law,

528
00:49:25,499 --> 00:49:28,064
so he made them stay at the rules; he told them;

529
00:49:28,126 --> 00:49:30,539
Okay, what if we find it in your belongings; what will happen?

530
00:49:30,721 --> 00:49:35,059
So they told him; their law; the law Yaqoob(يعقوب); which was you take him as a prisoner.

531
00:49:35,211 --> 00:49:39,199
He said: Okay, well follow your laws; sign this paper; this is the agreement.

532
00:49:39,548 --> 00:49:41,643
We are following your rules, not ours.

533
00:49:42,478 --> 00:49:48,829
And then they started looking in the camels one by one, and they started with the other camels before.

534
00:49:48,996 --> 00:49:53,456
So they kept on uncovering them, they would look inside, they would not find it, they would go to the next one.

535
00:49:53,646 --> 00:49:56,896
And then when they opened up the luggage of Binyamin(بنيامين) they found it there.

536
00:49:58,015 --> 00:50:05,275
When they found this cup in the luggage of Binyamin(بنيامين); what did the brothers say?

537
00:50:06,918 --> 00:50:19,603
قالوا إِن يَسرِق فَقَد سَرَقَ أَخٌ لَهُ مِن قَبلُ ۚ

538
00:50:19,987 --> 00:50:25,242
They said: If he steals his brother has stole before.

539
00:50:27,337 --> 00:50:31,037
They said that his brother stole before.

540
00:50:31,418 --> 00:50:32,752
They're talking about Yusuf(يوسُف).

541
00:50:33,680 --> 00:50:36,442
Now the Mufasireen(مفسرين) say: What is meant by this is that;

542
00:50:36,696 --> 00:50:40,687
When Yusuf(يوسُف) was young; look at the how they could twist the information.

543
00:50:41,029 --> 00:50:45,378
When Yusuf(يوسُف) was young he did steal; but what did he steal?

544
00:50:46,048 --> 00:50:50,510
His grandmother; they say, this is the story of Tafseer(تفسير), Allah Ho Alam(ألله أعلم); This could be valid or it could be not.

545
00:50:50,754 --> 00:51:01,662
It says that his grandmother had a small idle and Yusuf(يوسُف) stole it from her and he destroyed it.

546
00:51:03,366 --> 00:51:07,271
So they use this and they said, he stole before.

547
00:51:07,469 --> 00:51:12,133
Even though this is not really stealing, this is Da'wah(دعوة) destroying a false god.

548
00:51:13,268 --> 00:51:14,633
Anyway they said;

549
00:51:15,379 --> 00:51:17,943
إِن يَسرِق فَقَد سَرَقَ أَخٌ لَهُ مِن قَبلُ ۚ

550
00:51:18,959 --> 00:51:21,274
Let me read these Ayaat(آيات) that we just covered now.

551
00:51:21,688 --> 00:51:43,115
فَلَمّا جَهَّزَهُم بِجَهازِهِم جَعَلَ السِّقايَةَ في رَحلِ أَخيهِ ثُمَّ أَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ

552
00:51:45,687 --> 00:52:02,560
 ثُمَّ أَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ أَيَّتُهَا العيرُ إِنَّكُم لَسارِقونَ۝

553
00:52:02,694 --> 00:52:08,161
So when he had furnished them forth with their provisions he put the golden bowl into their brothers bag;

554
00:52:08,574 --> 00:52:12,312
then a crier cried, O you in the caravan surely you are thieves.

555
00:52:12,598 --> 00:52:25,840
قالوا وَأَقبَلوا عَلَيهِم ماذا تَفقِدونَ۝

556
00:52:26,507 --> 00:52:30,515
Then they turn toward them and said: What is it that you have missed?

557
00:52:30,594 --> 00:52:51,802
قالوا نَفقِدُ صُواعَ المَلِكِ وَلِمَن جاءَ بِهِ حِملُ بَعيرٍ وَأَنا بِهِ زَعيمٌ۝

558
00:52:52,304 --> 00:52:57,103
They said: We have missed the golden bowl of the king and for him, who produces it,

559
00:52:57,471 --> 00:53:01,042
the reward of a camel load; I will be bound by it.

560
00:53:01,217 --> 00:53:23,010
قالوا تَاللَّهِ لَقَد عَلِمتُم ما جِئنا لِنُفسِدَ فِي الأَرضِ وَما كُنّا سارِقينَ۝

561
00:53:23,437 --> 00:53:29,597
They said: By Allah Indeed you know that we came not to make mischeif in the land, and we are no thieves.

562
00:53:30,162 --> 00:53:45,445
قالوا فَما جَزاؤُهُ إِن كُنتُم كاذِبينَ۝

563
00:53:46,246 --> 00:53:48,334
They, Joseph's men said;

564
00:53:48,660 --> 00:53:53,176
What then shall be the penalty of him, if you are proved to be liars.

565
00:53:53,541 --> 00:54:08,001
قالوا جَزاؤُهُ مَن وُجِدَ في رَحلِهِ فَهُوَ جَزاؤُهُ ۚ

566
00:54:08,748 --> 00:54:10,524
They said; The brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف);

567
00:54:10,770 --> 00:54:19,225
The penalty should be that; in whose bag it is found should be held for the punishment of the crime thus we punish the wrongdoers.

568
00:54:19,645 --> 00:54:40,921
فَبَدَأَ بِأَوعِيَتِهِم قَبلَ وِعاءِ أَخيهِ ثُمَّ استَخرَجَها مِن وِعاءِ أَخيهِ ۚ

569
00:54:41,739 --> 00:54:45,080
So he began the search in their bags before the bag of his brother.

570
00:54:45,231 --> 00:54:47,318
Then he brought it out of his brother's bag.

571
00:54:47,532 --> 00:54:53,311
كَذٰلِكَ كِدنا لِيوسُفَ ۖ

572
00:54:55,946 --> 00:55:16,459
ما كانَ لِيَأخُذَ أَخاهُ في دينِ المَلِكِ إِلّا أَن يَشاءَ اللَّهُ ۚ

573
00:55:16,988 --> 00:55:23,427
Thus did we plan for Joseph; He could not take his brother by the law of the king.

574
00:55:23,641 --> 00:55:25,832
Except that Allah willed it.

575
00:55:26,697 --> 00:55:35,829
نَرفَعُ دَرَجاتٍ مَن نَشاءُ ۗ

576
00:55:36,551 --> 00:55:38,646
We raise the degrees whom He please.

577
00:55:38,861 --> 00:55:47,570
وَفَوقَ كُلِّ ذي عِلمٍ عَليمٌ۝

578
00:55:47,903 --> 00:55:52,488
But over all those endowed with knowledge is the all knowing Allah.

579
00:55:53,138 --> 00:55:54,742
I want to comment on one word here,

580
00:55:55,115 --> 00:55:58,194
ما كانَ لِيَأخُذَ أَخاهُ في دينِ المَلِكِ

581
00:55:58,575 --> 00:56:03,403
Allah says: He could not take his brother according to the religion of the king.

582
00:56:05,594 --> 00:56:08,379
Deen(دِيْن); Allah used the word Deen(دِيْن).

583
00:56:09,514 --> 00:56:12,916
Allah is calling this law Deen(دِيْن); It is religion.

584
00:56:13,837 --> 00:56:15,440
Laws are part of religion.

585
00:56:15,741 --> 00:56:19,693
This is a law; we call it criminal law here in the United States criminal law.

586
00:56:19,875 --> 00:56:21,280
It has nothing to do with religion.

587
00:56:21,661 --> 00:56:27,696
And that mentality is being engraved in our minds unfortunately, that laws have nothing to do with religion.

588
00:56:28,212 --> 00:56:33,502
Allah in Qur'an is calling the law of the king; Deen(دِيْن); religion, that is the religion of the king.

589
00:56:33,686 --> 00:56:36,781
And this is the religion of Allah; Laws are part of religion.

590
00:56:37,329 --> 00:56:38,053
في دينِ المَلِكِ

591
00:56:38,083 --> 00:56:41,091
Allah did not say in the Qanoon(قانون) of Malik(ملك) - in the law of the Malik(ملك).

592
00:56:41,121 --> 00:56:44,138
Allah say in the Deen(دِيْن), the religion of the Malik(ملك) the king.

593
00:56:45,329 --> 00:56:46,210
They said;

594
00:56:46,289 --> 00:56:59,115
قالوا إِن يَسرِق فَقَد سَرَقَ أَخٌ لَهُ مِن قَبلُ

595
00:56:59,415 --> 00:57:04,290
If he steals there was a brother of his who did steal before him.

596
00:57:06,041 --> 00:57:10,318
SayidinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) held those emotions in his heart and he didn't speak.

597
00:57:10,850 --> 00:57:22,277
فَأَسَرَّها يوسُفُ في نَفسِهِ وَلَم يُبدِها لَهُم ۚ

598
00:57:22,602 --> 00:57:27,675
But these things did Joseph keeping himself revealing not the secrets to them.

599
00:57:27,705 --> 00:57:29,762
He did not respond to this.

600
00:57:30,373 --> 00:57:32,724
And then he said also silently.

601
00:57:33,223 --> 00:57:50,254
قالَ أَنتُم شَرٌّ مَكانًا ۖ وَاللَّهُ أَعلَمُ بِما تَصِفونَ۝

602
00:57:50,424 --> 00:57:57,608
He said: Within himself; you are in worst case and Allah knows best the truth of what you are saying.

603
00:57:58,011 --> 00:58:02,804
They're speaking to Yusuf(يوسُف) and this they're telling him that Yusuf(يوسُف) stole before.

604
00:58:02,834 --> 00:58:03,915
Yusuf(يوسُف) knows the truth.

605
00:58:03,945 --> 00:58:07,810
He said: Allah Ho Alam(ألله أعلم); Allah knows better but he did not show that to them.

606
00:58:08,278 --> 00:58:11,910
Now the brothers are trying to free Binyamin(بنيامين)

607
00:58:11,940 --> 00:58:14,951
because they have given their father a promise that we'll come back with him.

608
00:58:15,134 --> 00:58:47,888
قالوا يا أَيُّهَا العَزيزُ إِنَّ لَهُ أَبًا شَيخًا كَبيرًا فَخُذ أَحَدَنا مَكانَهُ ۖ إِنّا نَراكَ مِنَ المُحسِنينَ۝

609
00:58:48,112 --> 00:58:52,514
They said: Oh ruler of the land, Verily he has a father who is old.

610
00:58:52,632 --> 00:58:56,336
So take one of us in his place; Indeed we think you are one of the good doers.

611
00:58:56,396 --> 00:58:59,275
He said: No! that will be oppression; that is wrong.

612
00:58:59,346 --> 00:59:00,826
How can we take an innocent one?

613
00:59:01,017 --> 00:59:03,120
He is guilty; We're going to keep him.

614
00:59:04,144 --> 00:59:05,175
When they gave up;

615
00:59:05,620 --> 00:59:06,550
  خَلَصوا نَجِيًّا ۖ

616
00:59:06,610 --> 00:59:07,802
they went on the side.

617
00:59:08,850 --> 00:59:11,950
Their elder brother, they say his name is Robeel(روبيل).

618
00:59:12,234 --> 00:59:13,186
He said;

619
00:59:14,051 --> 00:59:44,606
قالَ كَبيرُهُم أَلَم تَعلَموا أَنَّ أَباكُم قَد أَخَذَ عَلَيكُم مَوثِقًا مِنَ اللَّهِ وَمِن قَبلُ ما فَرَّطتُم في يوسُفَ ۖ

620
00:59:47,110 --> 01:00:11,325
فَلَن أَبرَحَ الأَرضَ حَتّىٰ يَأذَنَ لي أَبي أَو يَحكُمَ اللَّهُ لي ۖ وَهُوَ خَيرُ الحاكِمينَ۝

621
01:00:11,744 --> 01:00:13,601
The eldest among them said;

622
01:00:13,903 --> 01:00:19,646
Know you not that your father did take an oath from you in Allah's name?

623
01:00:19,811 --> 01:00:23,045
And before this, you did fail in your duty with Yusuf(يوسُف).

624
01:00:23,585 --> 01:00:29,927
Therefore I will not leave this land, until my father permit me or Allah decides my case.

625
01:00:30,007 --> 01:00:31,580
And he is the best of the judges.

626
01:00:31,959 --> 01:00:35,972
He said: I am not going to leave Egypt, I'm not going to go and face my father after this.

627
01:00:36,322 --> 01:00:39,361
We have betrayed Yusuf(يوسُف) before.

628
01:00:39,480 --> 01:00:45,361
And now we're going to go to our father and say that our brother is taken as a prisoner; I'm not going to leave.

629
01:00:45,845 --> 01:00:48,892
So he stayed there, and the other brothers went back to Egypt.

630
01:00:49,162 --> 01:00:52,770
So they went back and they told their father what happened.

631
01:00:53,080 --> 01:00:54,715
The father didn't believe this.

632
01:00:55,032 --> 01:00:58,867
How could it happen that before you betrayed Yusuf(يوسُف) and you come and lie,

633
01:00:58,970 --> 01:01:02,883
and now you betray his other brother and you lie, so he told them;

634
01:01:03,327 --> 01:01:19,887
قالَ بَل سَوَّلَت لَكُم أَنفُسُكُم أَمرًا ۖ فَصَبرٌ جَميلٌ ۖ

635
01:01:20,316 --> 01:01:24,723
Nay but your own selves have be guilted you to do something.

636
01:01:26,223 --> 01:01:27,223
They said;

637
01:01:27,961 --> 01:01:51,811
وَاسأَلِ القَريَةَ الَّتي كُنّا فيها وَالعيرَ الَّتي أَقبَلنا فيها ۖ وَإِنّا لَصادِقونَ۝

638
01:01:52,300 --> 01:01:54,041
This time; they are telling the truth.

639
01:01:54,795 --> 01:02:01,075
They said: Ask the people in Egypt and ask the caravan of them or witness that we're telling the truth.

640
01:02:01,868 --> 01:02:06,816
But this is like they say that there was one Shepherd of sheep.

641
01:02:08,570 --> 01:02:12,994
And once he started saying the wolf was attacking, the wolf was attacking; so everybody came to help him.

642
01:02:14,057 --> 01:02:16,367
They found that there's no wolf he was lying.

643
01:02:16,851 --> 01:02:20,517
In the next day; He said the wolf is attacking the wolf as attacking, they all came to help him.

644
01:02:20,748 --> 01:02:21,807
Nobody came to help him.

645
01:02:22,284 --> 01:02:24,298
The third day the wolf did show up.

646
01:02:24,758 --> 01:02:29,083
And he started saying the wolf is attacking, the wolf is attacking; Nobody came to help him because they thought he is lying.

647
01:02:29,508 --> 01:02:33,337
So the brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف); they lied before, they lied about Yusuf(يوسُف).

648
01:02:33,885 --> 01:02:37,754
Now, they're telling the truth, but their fathers cannot believe it.

649
01:02:38,738 --> 01:02:41,587
And they're trying to convince him and they're telling them ask the witnesses.

650
01:02:41,617 --> 01:02:43,220
But he said: No.

651
01:02:43,325 --> 01:02:44,582
You have made the plot

652
01:02:45,169 --> 01:02:46,181
  فَصَبرٌ جَميلٌ ۖ

653
01:02:46,796 --> 01:02:49,773
He said: I will have patience.

654
01:02:50,654 --> 01:02:51,122
And then he said;

655
01:02:51,152 --> 01:02:53,430
عَسَى اللَّهُ أَن يَأتِيَني بِهِم جَميعًا

656
01:02:53,454 --> 01:02:54,419
He did not lose hope.

657
01:02:54,449 --> 01:02:57,414
He said: May Allah bring them all back to me.

658
01:02:57,512 --> 01:02:58,528
Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother.

659
01:02:58,687 --> 01:03:01,332
He did not even lose hope in Yusuf(يوسُف)

660
01:03:01,552 --> 01:03:06,536
because he remembers the dream of Yusuf(يوسُف) and he knows that one day Yusuf(يوسُف) will be victorious; he knew.

661
01:03:07,620 --> 01:03:14,413
The father; Now his sorrow; his injury was brought up again.

662
01:03:14,827 --> 01:03:17,911
And he remembered Yusuf(يوسُف) and now it's Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother Binyamin(بنيامين).

663
01:03:18,292 --> 01:03:22,530
So the father started to cry and weep; until he turned blind.

664
01:03:23,395 --> 01:03:25,155
He kept on crying and weeping.

665
01:03:25,339 --> 01:03:27,211
وَابيَضَّت عَيناهُ مِنَ الحُزنِ

666
01:03:27,421 --> 01:03:31,397
Until his eyes lost vision because of sorrow.

667
01:03:33,127 --> 01:03:34,387
فَهُوَ كَظيمٌ۝

668
01:03:34,643 --> 01:03:36,699
He was suppressing that sorrow.

669
01:03:38,199 --> 01:03:41,677
The brothers tried to reduce this pain on their father and they said;

670
01:03:41,707 --> 01:03:47,764
By Allah, you will never cease remembering Yusuf(يوسُف) until you become weak with old age or until you be of the dead.

671
01:03:48,127 --> 01:03:49,413
They felt sorry for their father.

672
01:03:49,473 --> 01:03:55,073
They saw that he's gonna destroy his health, by this sorrow that he's suppressing in his heart.

673
01:03:55,383 --> 01:03:56,200
He said;

674
01:03:56,573 --> 01:04:20,424
قالَ إِنَّما أَشكو بَثّي وَحُزني إِلَى اللَّهِ وَأَعلَمُ مِنَ اللَّهِ ما لا تَعلَمونَ۝

675
01:04:20,870 --> 01:04:27,828
I only complain of my grief and sorrow to Allah and I know from Allah that which you know not.

676
01:04:28,150 --> 01:04:31,047
I am not complaining to you I'm not complaining to mankind.

677
01:04:31,459 --> 01:04:33,706
I am asking Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to help me.

678
01:04:33,766 --> 01:04:35,095
  أشكو إلى الله

679
01:04:35,383 --> 01:04:37,748
I seek assistance from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

680
01:04:38,621 --> 01:04:39,529
And then he said;

681
01:04:40,129 --> 01:05:00,395
يا بَنِيَّ اذهَبوا فَتَحَسَّسوا مِن يوسُفَ وَأَخيهِ وَلا تَيأَسوا مِن رَوحِ اللَّهِ ۖ

682
01:05:01,176 --> 01:05:04,585
Oh my son's go you and inquire about Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother.

683
01:05:05,085 --> 01:05:08,856
The father is telling these other brothers go and look Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother.

684
01:05:09,364 --> 01:05:12,570
But Sayidina Yaqub عليه السلام did not lose hope and he said;

685
01:05:12,888 --> 01:05:19,613
And never give up hope of Allah's  mercy; certainly no one despair is of Allah's mercy except people who disbelief.

686
01:05:22,263 --> 01:05:24,859
صلى الله عليه وسلم على سيدنا محمد وعلى آله وصحبه وسلم

